---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { site, ext } from "../data/site";

const updated = "8 October 2026";
const issues = `${site.repo}/issues`;
const license = `${site.repo}/blob/main/LICENSE`;

const h2 = "mt-14 text-2xl md:text-3xl";
const p = "mt-4 max-w-2xl text-lg leading-relaxed text-paper/70";
const ul = "mt-4 max-w-2xl list-disc space-y-2 pl-6 text-lg leading-relaxed text-paper/70 marker:text-paper/30";
const link = "text-paper underline decoration-white/30 underline-offset-4 transition-colors hover:decoration-paper";
---
<Base title="Terms of Use" description="The rules for using Saya and this website.">
  <section class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-6 pt-20">
    <h1 class="text-4xl md:text-6xl">Terms of Use</h1>
    <p class="mt-4 text-paper/50">Last updated {updated}</p>
    <p class={p}>
      These terms apply to the {site.name} browser and to this website. By downloading, installing or using
      {site.name}, you agree to them. If you do not agree, please do not use it.
    </p>

    <h2 class={h2}>1. Who we are</h2>
    <p class={p}>
      {site.name} is developed and maintained by {site.owner} ("we", "us"). You can reach us through
      <a href={issues} class={link} {...ext(issues)}> GitHub</a>.
    </p>

    <h2 class={h2}>2. License</h2>
    <p class={p}>
      The source code of {site.name} is released under the
      <a href={license} class={link} {...ext(license)}> MIT license</a>. You may use, copy, modify and distribute it
      under the conditions of that license, which must be kept with any copy. Chromium, Electron and the other
      components bundled with {site.name} are under their own licenses, listed on the Credits page inside the browser
      (<span class="whitespace-nowrap">saya://credits</span>).
    </p>

    <h2 class={h2}>3. Beta software</h2>
    <p class={p}>
      {site.name} is under active development. Current builds are alpha or beta releases and may contain bugs,
      change without notice, or lose settings. Builds are not code-signed yet, so Windows SmartScreen may show a
      warning. Verify the checksum from the release notes before choosing "Run anyway". Please keep a backup of
      anything important, such as bookmarks.
    </p>

    <h2 class={h2}>4. Using {site.name}</h2>
    <ul class={ul}>
      <li>You are responsible for the websites you visit, the files you download and what you do with them.</li>
      <li>You agree not to use {site.name} to break the law or to harm other people or systems.</li>
      <li>You may not misrepresent a modified version of {site.name} as the official one.</li>
      <li>Keep your computer and your Windows account secure. Local data (history, cookies, bookmarks) is readable by anyone with access to your account.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 class={h2}>5. Ad blocker and filters</h2>
    <p class={p}>
      The built-in ad blocker uses filter lists maintained by third parties. Blocking can occasionally break a
      website, hide content you wanted, or let some ads through. You can pause it for any site. We do not control
      those lists and are not responsible for their contents or availability.
    </p>

    <h2 class={h2}>6. Third-party websites and services</h2>
    <p class={p}>
      {site.name} connects you to services we do not own or control: websites, search engines and DNS providers.
      Your use of them is governed by their own terms and privacy policies. Details of what is sent to them are in our
      <a href="/privacy" class={link}> Privacy Policy</a>.
    </p>

    <h2 class={h2}>7. No warranty</h2>
    <p class={p}>
      {site.name} is provided "as is" and "as available", without warranty of any kind, whether express or implied,
      including fitness for a particular purpose, merchantability, security, or that it will be uninterrupted or
      error-free. Browsing the web always carries risk, and no browser can guarantee protection from every threat.
    </p>

    <h2 class={h2}>8. Limitation of liability</h2>
    <p class={p}>
      To the fullest extent permitted by law, {site.owner} is not liable for any indirect, incidental or
      consequential damages, or for loss of data, profits or access, arising from the use of or inability to use
      {site.name}. Nothing in these terms excludes liability that cannot be excluded by law.
    </p>

    <h2 class={h2}>9. This website</h2>
    <p class={p}>
      The content of this website is provided for information about {site.name}. We may change or remove it at any
      time. Links to other sites are for convenience and do not mean we endorse them.
    </p>

    <h2 class={h2}>10. Changes</h2>
    <p class={p}>
      We may update these terms as {site.name} evolves. The date at the top shows the latest revision. Continuing to
      use {site.name} after a change means you accept the updated terms.
    </p>

    <h2 class={h2}>11. Governing law</h2>
    <p class={p}>These terms are governed by the laws of the Republic of Indonesia. Any dispute should first be raised with us so we can try to resolve it informally.</p>

    <h2 class={h2}>12. Contact</h2>
    <p class={p}>
      Questions about these terms:
      <a href={issues} class={link} {...ext(issues)}> open an issue on GitHub</a>.
    </p>
  </section>
</Base>
